/-!
# Certificates for the descent of `CoverDescent.lean`

Generated by `scripts/cover_descent/lean_cert.py`; do not edit by hand.

* `masks`: for each modulus used, the squares and the Gaussian squares modulo it, as bit masks;
  `mask8`, …: each mask is the one computed by `sMask`, `gMask` (evaluated by the kernel).
* `table`: for each ratio `m : n`, the primes of `2mn(m − n)(m + n)` and a certificate: lines
  `(p, k, c)` saying that modulo `p^k` the candidates at the bits of `c` are excluded (for
  `k = 0`: modulo the prime `p`, by the criterion of Euler, `killsE`). The
  candidates are the products of those of the primes that are 2 or `≡ ±1 (mod 8)` (Theorem E,
  `exists_class_prod8`). `table_ok`: every entry passes `entryOk8` (evaluated by the kernel, in
  pieces `chunk0`, …).
* `table4`: certificates with one class for each form (`entryOk4`), for the ratios that have no
  certificate with one class.
* `structTable`, `class_of_mem_structTable`: for 150 ratios with a degenerate solution, among them
  `627 : 364` and `991 : 263` (class `521266`), the class of every solution, from the theorems on
  the class alone (`structOk`).
* `no_fullSquares_of_mem_ratios`: for the ratios of the two tables, no rational `t` makes the
  five free cells of the G1 family squares.
* `IsMSS.ratio_ne_of_coverDescent`, `IsMSS.ratio_ne_of_le_1000_descent`: the same for a magic
  square of squares; with the census by residue classes, for coprime `1 ≤ n < m ≤ 1000` the ratio
  is one of the pairs of `exceptions`, and `m² + n²` is a square or twice a square
  (`exceptions_degenerate`, `IsMSS.ratio_norm_sq_or_two_sq_of_le_1000`).

No `native_decide`: every check is `decide +kernel`.
-/

